  "public_messages": [
    "I\u2019ll read the workspace brief, feedback, memory instructions, and current source first. Then I\u2019ll trace the measured failure paths, make the smallest justified changes, and run the requested focused and race checks while keeping any test process inside this workspace.",
    "The feedback shows a single correctness failure: a migrated v1 idempotency key accepts a changed command (`200` instead of `409`). The latency figures are diagnostic because that gate failed. I\u2019m narrowing the fix to migration/replay command comparison, while checking the claim and mutation SQL/index paths for measured or obvious repeated work.",
    "I found a concrete replay gap: when the stored command contains newer fields, the legacy fallback checked only queue, payload, and max attempts, then checked the incoming request against assumed defaults. It never compared the stored priority, schedule, or retry base. That can turn a changed command into a replay. I\u2019ll compare every resolved command field on both sides; the failed-gate load data does not justify a throughput change, so I\u2019ll leave WAL/FULL durability and the current indexing strategy intact.",
    "The focused regression run exposed a compatibility condition in the supplied migration test: older serialized inputs can contain `retry_base_ms: 0` even though the original call omitted that field. I\u2019m adjusting the comparison to treat that stored zero as the legacy omitted value when replaying the legacy default, while still comparing nonzero stored scheduling values.",
    "The replay fix now preserves the supplied v1 replay case and rejects a changed priority/schedule/retry command; the focused check and `go test -race ./...` pass. The normal build also returned successfully in the parallel check. I\u2019m recording these verified actions in the bounded task checkpoint and confirming the final diff/build artifact.",
    "Fixed legacy idempotency replay comparison in [queue.go](<WORKSPACE>/internal/queue/queue.go): replay now compares stored priority, schedule, and retry base as well as the original fields. A serialized legacy retry value of zero still replays when the request omitted that field. Added a regression test in [queue_test.go](<WORKSPACE>/internal/queue/queue_test.go).\n\nThe focused replay and migration checks passed, as did `go test -race ./...`, `go build -o bin/queueforge ./cmd/server`, and `git diff --check`. Go 1.26.3 was used; `go.mod` and `go.sum` are unchanged. No server was started.\n\nFEEDBACK.json\u2019s independent migration scenario failed, and all six load artifacts had `artifact_gate_pass: false`. Their latency results are diagnostic, so I made no throughput change; WAL and `synchronous=FULL` remain intact. The genuine stage1 API scenario was not rerun, so the repair against its historical command encoding remains unconfirmed. The bounded memory checkpoint was updated and inspected at version 6."
  ],
